=== ROOM 55: THE SYSTEM INSPECTOR ===

You've entered an uncharted system. Your mission: identify it
completely using system inspection commands.

MISSION:
1. Run: uname -a  (get full system information)
2. Run: hostname  (get system name)
3. Run: id        (get your user identity)
4. Run: who       (see logged-in sessions)
5. Submit: ./getKey.sh "$(whoami)" "$(uname -s)"
   This passes your username and OS kernel name.

KEY COMMANDS:
   uname -a               All system info
   uname -r               Kernel release version
   uname -m               Machine hardware (x86_64, arm64)
   uname -s               Kernel name (Linux, Darwin)
   hostname               Show system hostname
   hostname -I            Show all IP addresses
   whoami                 Print effective username
   id                     Show uid, gid, groups
   id -u                  Just the numeric uid
   id -un                 Just the username
   who                    Show logged-in users
   w                      Who + what they're running
   last -n 5              Last 5 logins
   lscpu                  CPU architecture details
   cat /etc/os-release    Linux distribution info

To decrypt room_56 when you have the password:
   openssl enc -aes-256-cbc -d -a -pbkdf2 \
     -in ../room_56/README -out ../room_56/README.txt -pass pass:PASSWORD
   cat ../room_56/README.txt
